From: OpenWrt Build System <openwrt@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-drv: reject auto_scale work before core init

The frequency sysctls are registered before probe-gated NSS cores have
finished booting. A write in that window can queue work against
uninitialized resources. The current_freq handler already has this guard
(in fused 012); add the same check to nss_auto_scale_handler.

Source: VIKINGYFY/immortalwrt patch 017 (partial backport).

--- a/nss_init.c
+++ b/nss_init.c
@@ -259,6 +259,9 @@ static int nss_auto_scale_handler(const
 		return ret;
 	}

+	if (nss_top_main.nss[NSS_CORE_0].state != NSS_CORE_STATE_INITIALIZED)
+		return ret;
+
 	if (nss_cmd_buf.auto_scale != 1) {
 		/*
 		 * Disable frequency scaling, but keep core stats reporting
